  "id": "COMPOUND:17174 - PROTEIN:5840",
  "verbalization": "Melilitocarpan B appears to share a common target, SNU1, with multiple compounds that are involved in the regulation of H9. The evidence suggests that Melilitocarpan B may act through a pathway that involves SNU1, which is a target of several other compounds, including 3-(Hydroxyacetyl)Indole and 1-(6-Hydroxy-2-propan-2-yl-1-benzofuran-5-yl)ethanone, both of which have a target relationship with H9. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting SNU1, each with a unique structure, indicates that Melilitocarpan B may interact with SNU1 through a mechanism that is not yet fully understood. The integration of these pathways suggests that Melilitocarpan B could be part of a broader network of compounds that influence H9 through SNU1, potentially through a shared or distinct molecular mechanism. The evidence supports the idea that Melilitocarpan B may play a role in the regulation of H9 via a pathway involving SNU1, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
